earch to save  people lives with severe brain diseases  so this was from our view the complete  opposite so when you found out that it  was being used what was the company's  response from the beginning we were  against it as I said it's a clear  mission for us to improve people's lives  and we saw that as asset so what we  could do from the beginning was sending  letters to the prisons and we urged them  to stop them issues of our product with  a cooperative were they not cooperative  we never heard back from them so they  just ignored your letter they they  ignored us you know you have other  situations where you have misuse of  medication when people using medication  for doping and here if that's the case  you can work with authorities to try to  stop it but in this case it was actually  the authorities that was doing the  misuse the company restricted  distribution of pentobarbital and then  the European Union banned the export of  drugs which could be used in executions  eventually American prisons had to find  alternatives or get compounding  pharmacies to replicate those they could  no longer get their hands on a drug  called my dazzling took the place of  pentobarbital but it quickly became  controversial because critics  it isn't strong enough to properly  anesthetize a prisoner before the  subsequent drugs which paralyze and then  kill as evidence they cited executions  in Oklahoma and Arizona where the  process took longer than it should have  done  Robert Dunham runs the death penalty  Information Center you've got inmates  who are conscious  you've got inmates who are gasping one  of the descriptions was that the inmate  was flopping around like a fish against  the restraints that's someone who is  clearly experiencing high levels of pain  and we know that the the lethal drug is  akin to being burned from the inside out  here's one of Richard gossips attorneys  mark Henrickson for better for worse  than the death penalty was carried out  with lethal in